{"created": "2026-10-02T12:05:19.002195+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-02T15:11:52.050462+00:00", "id": 23102265, "conceptrecid": "23102264", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23102265", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23102264", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23102265", "metadata": {"title": "Strict Log-Concavity Across All Scales for Exact-Height Plane Binary Trees", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23102265", "publication_date": "2026-10-02", "description": "<p><span>&lt;p&gt;Let B&lt;sub&gt;0&lt;/sub&gt;(x) = x, B&lt;sub&gt;h+1&lt;/sub&gt;(x) = x(1 + B&lt;sub&gt;h&lt;/sub&gt;(x))&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; and N&lt;sub&gt;h&lt;/sub&gt; = B&lt;sub&gt;h&lt;/sub&gt; &minus; B&lt;sub&gt;h&minus;1&lt;/sub&gt;: N&lt;sub&gt;k,h&lt;/sub&gt; counts rooted plane binary trees with k vertices and exact height h. We prove that for every sufficiently large h the coefficient column is strictly log-concave on its whole interior, N&lt;sub&gt;k,h&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; &amp;gt; N&lt;sub&gt;k&minus;1,h&lt;/sub&gt;N&lt;sub&gt;k+1,h&lt;/sub&gt; for h+2 &le; k &le; 2&lt;sup&gt;h+1&lt;/sup&gt;&minus;2. The proof passes through eight asymptotic regimes &mdash; left edge, subcritical saddle, critical h&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; law, quasi-pole corridor, h&lt;sup&gt;3&lt;/sup&gt; crossover, supercritical Fatou&ndash;B&ouml;ttcher regime, bulk and right edge &mdash; sewn together on explicit windows.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Status.&lt;/strong&gt; Working preprint. The proof was developed with substantial assistance from AI systems; it has been checked internally (exact computation, symbolic verification of fragile identities) but has not yet been read by a specialist in analytic combinatorics. The theorem is eventual: no explicit h&lt;sub&gt;0&lt;/sub&gt; is given. Exact computation confirms the inequality for every h &le; 16 (two independent implementations: h &le; 12 and h &le; 16).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The polynomials B&lt;sub&gt;h&lt;/sub&gt; enumerate the subsets closed under doubling of the complete binary trees in the 2-adic lifting of doubling modulo n (papers III&ndash;IV, doi:10.5281/zenodo.23088601).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Licences.&lt;/strong&gt; Text: CC BY 4.0. Code: AGPL v3; commercial licence on request.&lt;/p&gt;</span></p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Amiot, Anibal Edelberto", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0009-0002-6414-9448"}], "keywords": ["binary trees", "tree height", "log-concavity", "analytic combinatorics", "polynomial iteration", "saddle-point method", "Flajolet\u2013Odlyzko"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.23088601", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}], "version": "1.0.0", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "alternate_identifiers": [{"identifier": "Q141191562"}], "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23102264"}}]}, "notes": "<p><span>Code under AGPL v3. Commercial licence: anibaledel@gmail.com</span></p>"}, "title": "Strict Log-Concavity Across All Scales for Exact-Height Plane Binary Trees", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23102265", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23102265", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23102265?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23102265", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23102265", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23102265", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23102265/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23102264", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23102264", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23102264", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23102264", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23102265/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org